<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Operation Trident</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; December 4th 1971 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Indian West Coast &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; India &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the Indo-Pakistani conflict almost the entire Pakistan Navy fleet was based at Karachi Harbour, the headquarters of the Pakistani Navy. Karachi was also an important port for Pakistani maritime trade, critical for Pakistan’s economy. As such, the Karachi harbour was heavily defended against any air or naval strikes, and received the best defensive weapons in Pakistan's inventory in addition to being covered by two military air bases.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On the second night of the Indo-Pakistani War of 1971, the Indian Navy launched a fast naval strike on the Pakistan Naval Headquarters at Karachi. Lacking strike range, four Indian Navy Vidyut-class (Osa I) missile boats were towed towards Karachi by a fleet tanker, escorted by two anti-submarine Arnala-class (Petya III) corvettes. Once in position south of the harbour, and supported by one of the Arnala-class ships, the three of the four missile boats began their attack.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
